Horseshit!  There's nothing inherently wrong with being rude and obnoxious;
indeed, those adjectives are defined individually.  What is rude and obnoxious
to you or to me may be "right on the money" to someone else.  Inherently
threatening?  To whom?  People with extraordinarily sensitive egos?  I have
a lot of difficulty feeling threatened by bellicose words on a computer screen,
especially words directed at a segment of the population rather than at an
individual.  The last I checked, the first amendment to the Constitution of
the United States protects free speech and free press, and I should suppose
that postings to the Internet would qualify as some amalgam of those two
rights.  While use of the Internet may not be a right, but a privilege, I
would suggest that once that privilege has been granted, to revoke the
privilege or otherwise punish the individual for a posting which some (or many,
or most, or all) consider offensive would be unjustifiable under the
Constitution.  Especially in light of the fact that people cite the same
Constitution to protect non-existent rights such as "privacy" and "freedom of
expression," free speech is a right which must be protected regardless of the
medium by which it is transmitted.

