If the organization is subject to frequent such attacks, this is 
even more reason that the ~ftp/etc/passwd file shouldn't contain 
real passwords.  It should contain only uid's and logins, only 
marginally useful for crackers.  The real system password file 
shouldn't ever be available for anonymous ftp.
