I'm glad Bernie recognizes, here and elsewhere in his posting, that he's
proposing *new* conventions: changing the way ordinary users, and probably
sysadmins as well, are expected to behave.

What he hasn't made clear is _why_.  What circumstances mandate a change in
anonymous ftp conventions?  There have been a lot of changes in the network
population in recent years, and changes in the typical network user's
personal profile.  But so far as I'm aware, there hasn't been one single
significant incident attributable to people ftp'ing files in ~ftp they
shouldn't.  Files stored in ~ftp by a sysadmin, that is.

There have been some incidents involving people storing pornographic GIF's
