I counsel students not to use Webster in discussing concepts that possess
a conceptual meaning where at least minimal precision is required.
When the term "pirate" is bandied about so loosely, yet used to
pejoratize the character and arguments of others, it helps to establish
the meanings a bit more clearly. At stake are the limits of acceptable
fair use, the limits of authors' and users' rights, the gray area between
infringement and/or theft, and the obligations that authors and users
have to one another. 

